+      "description": "The retained resolution read-set layout a TypeScript context commits to when nodeModulesInReadSet is true. One row per installed package DIRECTORY inside the project that the resolver may read: installPath is the project-relative directory as the resolver walks it, realPath is the project-relative directory after symlink/workspace-link resolution (equal to installPath when there is no link), and contentSha256 is the raw SHA-256 of that package directory manifest file bytes (its package.json) as RETAINED, joined by digest (the blobJoin on the native.context.typescript.v2 nested record, native-evidence section 2.2). A layout ROW is a package-directory resolution observation, not itself a snapshot inventory row. The FILES the analysis actually read inside a listed package directory ARE snapshot inventory rows (identity-and-evidence section 3 'What sourceInventory contains'; native-evidence section 1.4 U-4/U-4a): they have membership syntax-only / host-ignore-convention, are retained under their inventory digests, and Run closure joins each such row to the installPath or realPath of a row of this record, refusing SNAPSHOT_PRUNED_TREE_NOT_A_READ otherwise. Unread material in an installed dependency tree is never inventoried. This record commits package-directory granularity only: which files inside a listed package were read is a host TCB observation. Required inputs read from OUTSIDE the project root, such as compiler library files and the TypeScript standard library, stay in their owning toolchain and stdlib closures and are never snapshot paths. An earlier description said no inventory row could exist for files in these directories; that contradicted the selected read-set law and is superseded. Rows are strictly ascending and unique by installPath, so one layout has one spelling. nodeModulesLayoutDigest is the raw SHA-256 of C(this record); it is null exactly when nodeModulesInReadSet is false."
